==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|sco|Swethin}}, {{m|sco|Swadne}} (also {{m|sco|Swaden}}), from {{der|en|dum|Sweden}}, dative of {{m|dum|Swede}}. Originally used to refer to the people before the late 1600s, later displaced native {{ncog|ang|Swēoland|lit=Swede land}}, {{m|ang|Swēoþēod|lit=Swede nation}}, and {{m|ang|Swēorīċe|lit=Swede kingdom}} to refer to the country.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=195631|date=December 2020}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=n}}</ref><ref>{{R:Etymonline}}</ref>

